{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The driver's own trace places him inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius for a continuous qualifying run of 200 seconds — 21 consecutive in-radius fixes running from 21:23:45 to 21:27:05 — which discharges POL-NS-01 limbs (a) to (c): there is a driver 'arrived' event at 21:23:45, the trace places him inside the geofence at that timestamp, and he held position for longer than the 180-second free waiting period in force for this trip (platform_policy.free_wait_sec, and not the pre-version-2 minimum_dwell_sec).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02724", "EV-TRIP-02724"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The waiting-period arithmetic closes in the driver's favour: the effective in-geofence dwell of 200 seconds exceeds the 180-second free waiting period by 20 seconds, so there is no shortfall and POL-NS-06's premature-cancellation refund is not licensed on this record. The accumulation limb POL-NS-06(i) is unavailable in any event — EV-ADVIS-02724-01 is MISSING (MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight 0.0, no payload), so there is no advisory covering the pickup road — and the driver does not rely on it; its absence is evidence neither for nor against him.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02724", "EV-TRIP-02724", "EV-ADVIS-02724-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.accumulated_dwell.shortfall_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The 'arrived' marker is not a false one. The derived arrival returns dwell_start_offset_sec of 0.0, meaning the first qualifying in-geofence fix falls at the timestamp of the driver's arrival event itself; the driver was therefore not still 300 m out and not travelling at or above 15 km/h when he tapped 'I'm Here', so POL-NS-05 does not recompute the waiting clock and no false-arrival referral attaches to him.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02724", "EV-TRIP-02724"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.dwell_start_offset_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing in the driver's profile engages POL-NS-07's anti-farming gate: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1, below the 4 the clause requires, and 1 over 120 completed trips is a rate of 0.008, far below the 0.08 the clause also requires (the test needs both limbs). Compensation may not be withheld on profile grounds, and the lifetime prior_no_show_flags counter on the same profile is not the field POL-NS-07 reads and may not be substituted for it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-02724"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No escalation trigger under POL-NS-09 is present on this record: every artifact that carries the arrival, dwell or rider-presence facts is COMPLETE at weight 1.0, no two admissible artifacts contradict each other directly on arrival, dwell or presence, the parties have no no-show dispute history between them (disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0 on both profiles) and rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0. The case is therefore decidable on its merits and should not be held.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02724", "EV-TRIP-02724", "EV-RPROF-02724", "EV-DPROF-02724"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "If the fee is held chargeable, the driver's entitlement is the net figure POL-NS-07 fixes — 80 per cent of the $4.50 cancellation fee, that is $3.60 — which is the very figure the fare ledger's own money block computes under POL-NS-07, and on such a ruling the emitted value is DRIVER_COMPENSATION with amount_sgd mirroring the driver payment and the rider's charge standing as the disposition of the fee.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02724", "EV-TRIP-02724"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver does not press the fee on the footing that this was a rider no-show, and does not stretch the record to do so: the cancellation is recorded under DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE, which POL-NS-01 limb (d) states in terms does not satisfy that limb, and the rider's own device also places her stationary within roughly 14 m of the pin through the waiting window. The concession is confined to that limb — the driver asks only that the record show his arrival, his full 200-second wait and his clean 30-day no-show record, and that the adverse entry be the single driver-education referral the clause provides for a mis-selected reason code, with no false-arrival or fee-farming finding added to it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02724", "EV-GPS-02724"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.5,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-01: driver-education item — the trip was terminated under the mis-selected reason code DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE while the driver's stationary fixes lay inside the POL-NS-02 arrival radius; record the mis-selected reason code against driver DRV-09724 for driver education."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "This dispute concerns the SGD 4.50 cancellation fee charged to the rider after the driver cancelled trip TRP-02724 at 21:27:08 under reason code DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE. The rider is refunded the whole SGD 4.50, and no driver compensation is payable.\n\nDriver — most of your account is accepted. Your GPS trace (EV-GPS-02724, weight 1.0) places you inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius from 21:23:45, the timestamp of your 'I'm Here' tap, and holds you there for a continuous run of 21 qualifying fixes lasting 200 seconds — longer than the 180-second free waiting period in force (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec, EV-TRIP-02724). Your arrival marker was not false: the first qualifying in-geofence fix coincides with the arrival event (dwell_start_offset_sec 0.0), so POL-NS-05 does not recompute the waiting clock and no false-arrival referral attaches. Your profile also raises no anti-farming bar (no_show_terminations_30d is 1, below the 4 POL-NS-07 requires, and 1 over 120 completed trips is 0.008, below the 0.08 also required — both limbs must hold). But none of that decides the fee. POL-NS-01 is conjunctive: limb (d) requires termination for RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE or EXCESSIVE_WAIT, and DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE — as you acknowledge — is none of them; the clause names it as the driver's own admission that he could not find the rider. Because your stationary fixes lie inside the arrival radius, POL-NS-01 fixes the outcome: the fee is not chargeable, the rider is refunded in full, and no compensation is payable. Your claim for the SGD 3.60 net figure under POL-NS-07 therefore fails: POL-NS-07 pays only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full or POL-NS-10(g) applies, and neither condition holds. The lifetime prior_no_show_flags field on your profile was correctly not used for anything — it is not the field POL-NS-07 reads.\n\nRider — you also succeed independently under POL-NS-04. The chat log (EV-CHAT-02724, weight 1.0) shows your locating message 'at the lift lobby' at 21:24:45 inside the waiting window; the driver neither replied within 120 seconds nor placed an in-app call (trip_record.in_app_calls is empty) before cancelling 143 seconds later; and your own device track (EV-GPS-02724) was within the 100 m rider-presence radius for all 43 qualifying fixes, maximum 17.74 m from the pin. POL-NS-04 likewise refunds the fee in full with no driver compensation.\n\nAmount: the fare breakdown (EV-FARE-02724, weight 1.0) records total_charged 4.50, a single cancellation_fee line of 4.50, payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00. The trip never started — no distance fare, time fare, waiting-time fee, booking fee, ERP or surcharge — so the whole contested amount is the cancellation fee, and SGD 4.50 is returned to the rider. The monetary effect (SGD 4.50) is below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of SGD 8.00, so this refund executes automatically on issue.\n\nThe traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-02724-01) is MISSING and carries weight 0.0; it was cited by both sides only for its absence. It cannot carry any fact, but its absence is itself citable, and POL-NS-06(i) — which requires a present and populated advisory of an admissible type — is not available to excuse or extend anything here, and nothing rested on it. No artifact deciding this case is impaired: the GPS trace, trip record, chat log and fare breakdown are all COMPLETE at weight 1.0, with 100 percent trace coverage, no gaps, intact chat sequence numbering and a cancellation line reconciling to the figure in force, so no POL-NS-08 discount and no POL-GEN-02 confidence cap below 1.0 applies. No contradiction between admissible artifacts, no disputes-with-counterparty history and no anti-farming trip on either profile engages POL-NS-09, so the case is decided rather than held."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
